        <body>
            <div xml:id="d353">

                <pb facs="d353-01" n="1" xml:id="d353-01"/>

                <head>353. Telegram 216018 From the Department of State to the Mission to the United
                        Nations<anchor n="1" xml:id="d353-f1"/>
                    <anchor n="2" xml:id="d353-f2"/>
                </head>
                <dateline><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                        when="1972-11-29T18:12:00+00:00">November 29, 1972, 1812Z</date>.</dateline>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>Subj:</label>
                    <item>Non-use of Force (NUF) Res</item>
                </list>
                <list type="references">
                    <head>Refs:</head>
                    <item>(A) USUN 4880; (B) State 207841; (C) State 215438</item>
                </list>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>USDel instructed to abstain in plenary vote on revised non-aligned NUF res
                        (reftel A).</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>USDel should ask for separate vote on sixth preambular para and vote
                        against.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>In explanation of vote on res you should include statement that US
                        considers that nothing in sixth or seventh preambular paras can change
                        Charter provisions regarding legitimate use of force.</item>
                    <label>4.</label>
                    <item>USDel should also add statement to effect that preambular para 8 recalls
                        res which US opposed. Our opposition to that res remains unchanged
                        notwithstanding our abstention on NUF res as whole.</item>
                </list>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d353-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d353-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files 1970–1973, DEF 18–6.
                    Confidential; Immediate. Drafted by Black (IO/UNP); cleared in UNP, NEA/RA,
                    L/UNA, EUR/SOV, NEA, UNP, PM/DCA, and ACDA/IR; and approved by De Palma of
                    IO.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d353-f2" n="2" xml:id="d353-f2-content">
                <p>The telegram instructed the U.S. delegation to abstain from voting on a revised
                    non-use of force resolution.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
